const memory = `Meridian Credits credit agreement, current release 1.0. Source: Finance approval recorded in issue trial-wsb (bd show trial-wsb), the initial agreement; no additional rationale was supplied. Preserve this complete policy for future statement features, beyond the single-line quote implemented in this issue.

Input and scope: The local standard-library Python CLI (python3 main.py) reads one JSON object on stdin and emits exactly one JSON object on stdout. No network, clock, locale, or third-party package is needed. Malformed input is outside the issue scope. A charge line has exactly line_id, account_id, subscription_id, service_on, charge_cents. IDs are nonempty strings; line_id is unique within a request. Subscription identity is the pair (account_id, subscription_id): subscription_id can repeat under different accounts; a subscription may have several charge lines. service_on is a valid Gregorian YYYY-MM-DD from 2020-01-01 through 2099-12-31 inclusive. No line is excluded by its service date. charge_cents is a nonnegative integer in US cents. Each request is the complete charge set of one independently quoted monthly statement; caps apply within that set. Line collections may be empty. Lexicographic ID order is Unicode code-point order. JSON object key order is immaterial; responses must have exactly specified keys.

Release selection: Omitted release selects the current agreement (currently "1.0"); explicit supported release selects that version. Versions introduced by issues remain supported afterward. Public suites specify explicit releases and remain applicable after current agreement changes. Run introduced suites with python3 test_public.py --cases PATH.

Release 1.0 calculation: Each line has an uncapped credit of 10% of charge_cents, rounded down separately to integer cents. The 2400-cent credit cap is shared by all lines with the same account_id across all its subscriptions; distinct accounts have independent caps. Within each account, allocate credit in ascending service_on order, breaking date ties by ascending line_id. Each line receives its uncapped credit up to the remaining account cap; later lines receive only the remaining credit or zero. Total credit is the sum of assigned line credits. A line amount due equals its charge minus assigned credit. Total due equals total charges minus total credit.

Single-line interface: {"command":"quote","line":LINE}, optionally with "release":"1.0", treats the supplied line as the entire statement and returns exactly release ("1.0"), line_id (copied), credit_cents, amount_due_cents. Example: charge 19999 yields credit 1999 and due 18000. Preserve {"command":"ping"} -> {"status":"ok","product":"Meridian Credits"} and existing unknown-command response {"error":"unknown_command"}. Behavior for unsupported releases is not specified in trial-wsb.

Verification for trial-wsb: python3 test_public.py --cases public_tests/release_1_quote.json passed. python3 -m unittest discover -s tests passed, including ping/unknown preservation and quote checks for omitted/explicit release, zero charges, per-line flooring, cap boundaries, very large integer charges, Unicode line_id preservation, and both service date endpoints. Multi-line allocation is approved policy, not implemented or tested by this single-line issue.`;
const quote = s => "'" + s.replace(/'/g, "'\\''") + "'";
text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:"bd remember "+quote(memory)+" --key meridian-credits-agreement",max_output_tokens:2000}));
